-- title:
--   Orthonormalization Measurement Right Of Consistency From Projectivization Repair Heterogeneous
-- statement:
--   **The heterogeneous orthonormalization estimate for Bob's measurement.**
--
--   Let $H_A$ and $H_B$ be finite local index sets, let $\psi$ be normalized on $H_A\otimes H_B$, and let $A$ and $B$ be finite-outcome measurements on the two registers. If their constant families are $\zeta$-consistent under the uniform singleton question distribution, with $\zeta\ge0$, then there exists a projective submeasurement $P$ on $H_B$ such that the right placements of $B$ and $P$ obey
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SDDRel}_{\psi,\mathcal U_1}
--    \bigl(B^{\mathrm R},P^{\mathrm R};\,100\,\zeta^{1/4}\bigr).
--   $$
--
--   Thus Bob's measurement is replaced by a projective submeasurement on the same local register, with the explicit orthonormalization error. This is the Bob-side measurement repair used by `ProjStrat.sourceRoleRegisterTwoSidedProjectiveSubmeasurements`.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MakingMeasurementsProjective.orthonormalizationMeasurement_right_of_consistency_from_projectivizationRepair_heterogeneous`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
